@vkamn @ygurov could you review this IPv6/dual-stack WireGuard fix when you have a chance? I’m tagging you because you authored and reviewed the AWG 3.1 changes in these connection paths.

The PR fixes desktop address-family handling, IPv6 endpoint serialization in the Apple Network Extension, and a kill-switch rule that blocks the IPv6 VPN transport itself. A real macOS connection through an IPv6 endpoint now succeeds with the kill switch enabled; regression tests and the remaining platform-validation limitations are listed in the description.

